course: dictionary
lesson: 5084
title: Words about money: insurer
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An insurer is a company, or a person, that sells insurance. You pay them a small amount of money regularly, called a premium. If something you have insured is lost, damaged or stolen, the insurer pays you money to help.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «The Affordable Care Act, often called Obamacare, made insurers cover people who were already ill.» The words cover, insured and pay tell you an insurer agrees to take on the costs. Ask yourself: what kind of company would do that? It must be a company that sells insurance.
explain: Look out for common phrases: car insurer, home insurer, and claim from the insurer. A claim is when you ask the insurer to pay you. Whenever money is paid out after an accident or a loss, an insurer may be part of the story.
fact: An insurer is a company or person that sells insurance.
fact: Insurers is the plural: more than one insurer.
fact: You pay an insurer a small regular amount called a premium.
fact: An insurer pays out money if something you insured is lost, damaged or stolen.
fact: In «made insurers cover people who were already ill», insurers are the companies that agree to pay for people's care.
exercise: «The Affordable Care Act made insurers cover people who were already ill.» What is an insurer in this sentence? | A shop that sells food and drink | *A company that sells insurance and pays out when needed | A teacher who marks homework | A type of hospital bed
exercise: Mum says, «Our car insurer will pay if the car is stolen.» What will the insurer do? | *Pay money to help if the car is stolen | Give free sweets to every driver | Drive the car to school | Sell the car to a new owner
exercise: You pay an insurer a small regular amount of money. What is this amount called? | Pocket money | Prize | Profit | *Premium
test: Which is the plural of insurer? | insurer's | *insurers | insurerish | insurering
test: Your home insurer pays you money when what happens? | You learn a new word | You get a new haircut | *Your house is damaged or stolen | You go on holiday
exam: Which sentence uses insurer correctly? | The insurer ate my lunch at school. | Insurer is a colour of paint. | *After the crash, the car insurer paid for the new bumper. | I insurer my dinner every night.
